# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# ============================================================================
# THIS FILE CURRENTLY KEEPS THE WHOLE SITE OUT OF EVERY SEARCH INDEX.
#
# DELETE THE X-Robots-Tag BLOCK WHEN momentaura.store IS CONNECTED.
# Leaving it in place after go-live makes the real shop unfindable, silently,
# on a site whose whole problem is being found and believed. Nothing here can
# detect that: the header is correct today and wrong the moment the domain is
# connected, and the only difference between the two is a DNS change that
# happens outside this repo. verify.mjs prints a note on every build for as
# long as this block exists, which is the only reminder there is.
# ============================================================================
#
# The site deploys to the .pages.dev URL only. momentaura.store is registered
# and owned, and stays unconnected until there is real stock and photography.
# Google forming a first impression of a shop with five out-of-stock products
# and kraft placeholders is a cost that is paid once and is hard to undo, and
# a first impression is the entire subject of this build.
#
# canonical and the sitemap already name momentaura.store, which is correct and
# not a contradiction: they describe where the site lives, this describes
# whether to index what is being served. noindex is what makes the mismatch
# harmless in the meantime — a crawler that reads a canonical pointing at a host
# that is not serving would otherwise have nowhere to go.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is used rather than Disallow in robots.txt on purpose. Disallow
# stops a crawler reading the page, which also stops it reading a noindex, so a
# URL discovered from a link elsewhere can still be listed. noindex is read and
# obeyed.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
